course: dictionary
lesson: 9341
title: Spiralling: going round and getting worse
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Spiralling means moving in a spiral, going round and round in a curve. A spiral can get wider or narrower, and it often goes up or down. «A sycamore seed came spiralling down from the tree.» The seed turns round and round as it falls, so spiralling describes its path.
explain: Spiralling can also describe things that rise quickly and get out of control, like «spiralling prices». When prices are spiralling, they are going up fast. Spiralling can describe feelings too: «My worries were spiralling» means they grew bigger every time I thought about them.
explain: Use context to work out which meaning fits. Catastrophising means jumping from a small thing to the worst possible ending, and «spiralling» is when thoughts get worse and worse. Try your meaning in the sentence: if "getting worse and worse" makes sense, you have the right idea.
fact: Spiralling means moving in a spiral, going round and round in a curve.
fact: «Spiralling prices» means prices are rising quickly and getting out of control.
fact: «Spiralling down» means getting worse and worse, or going round and round as you go down.
fact: A sycamore seed comes spiralling down, and water goes spiralling down the plughole.
fact: Spiralling is the British spelling; the American spelling is spiraling.
exercise: «The sycamore seed came spiralling down from the tree.» What does spiralling mean here? | Flying straight up into the sky | Splashing into a puddle | Standing still in the wind | *Turning round and round in a curve as it falls
exercise: «Prices for food are spiralling this year.» What does spiralling mean here? | Staying the same for years | Falling slowly to the ground | *Rising quickly and getting out of control | Going round in a circle at the shop
exercise: «My worries were spiralling until I talked to Mum.» Which word shows the worries kept getting bigger? | *spiralling | talked | until | Mum
test: «Water went spiralling down the plughole.» What is the best meaning of spiralling here? | *Turning round and round as it goes down | Frozen solid in the pipe | Bubbling up over the sink | Running out in a straight line
test: Ella says, «My thoughts are spiralling, and I keep making them worse.» What does she mean? | Her thoughts are very quiet | Her thoughts have stopped completely | Her thoughts are about spirals in art class | *Her thoughts keep getting worse and worse
exam: «The costs of the trip were spiralling, so the school had to cancel it.» What does spiralling show? | *Costs rising fast and getting out of control | Costs being counted slowly | Costs paid in coins | Costs written in a spiral pattern on paper
